ell so close that back up like that  and now we're also going to do another  inside reverse fold of the neck probably  about halfway so what you want to do is  you want to take this bottom edge here  and you're going to fold it up until  it's perpendicular with the back of the  Swan just like that so you don't want it  down like that you want it perpendicular  so it should cross with the back of the  Swan like that then you make a crease  right about there should be fun and then  you're going to unfold it and then  you're going to do another inside  reverse fold here along that V that you  should see so just tuck this in words  like that  and now you're going to have to bend the  beak the other way with these two edges  so it should look something like this  and now to complete the head of the  origami swan we're going to do an  outside reverse fold of this portion  here just like we did for the bottom  portion here so to do that again we're  going to make a crease like this and  this part is completely up to you what  the angle you want for the head so fold  it like that and then unfold it open  these two edges like that and then fold  downwards on the head like this crease  it here along the back and you also want  to make sure that this beak is creased  downwards now like that so it should  look something like this and now all you  have to do is to fold down the wings a  little bit now this again is up to you  on how you want to do it I like to take  this edge fold it down so that it joins  with this edge make a crease do the same  with the other side and then also we  have these two triangles sticking up we  could just fold those down a little bit  also open the end of it by kind of  tugging on it and you can push down on  this point if you like and there you go  you have completed your origami swan

